/*
artnet.lcb - xTalk Builder (LCB) library for Art-Net (DMX512 lighting over
             UDP). The artnetxt member of the xTalk suite (born as the Art-Net
             third of ShowControl for OpenXTalk).

Art-Net is plain byte-packing over a UDP socket on port 6454, openly published
and royalty free. It needs no third-party library and no C shim: this whole
extension is LCB, so it has no native library, nothing to build per platform,
and runs wherever the engine runs.

Transport is the script's own datagram socket, as for oscxt: build a packet
here and `write` the Data to "host:6454", on a socket opened first
(examples/artnet-helpers.livecodescript does both). Inbound packets arrive
through `accept datagram connections on port 6454 with message ...`; pass the
Data to artnetParseDmx or artnetParseReply. Nothing here starts a thread or
calls back into script.

THE ONE REAL GOTCHA -- mixed endianness:
  * OpCode is LITTLE-endian (low byte first): 0x5000 -> bytes 00 50.
  * Protocol version is BIG-endian (high byte first): 14 -> bytes 00 0E.
  * The ArtDmx Length is BIG-endian.
  * The ArtPollReply Port is LITTLE-endian again: 6454 -> bytes 36 19.
Reverse a big-endian field and a node silently ignores the packet. The shared
vectors (tests/vectors/artnet.json) pin every byte, and a clean-room codec
written from the specification (tools/sim/refcodec.py) agrees with them.

Nothing here throws for bad INPUT: a refusal returns an empty result and
artnetLastError() says why. An EMPTY value into a typed parameter is the
engine's error, raised before any code here runs (the suite's engine note 6.4),
and a fractional universe is cut toward zero where it becomes a byte (6.17).

Art-Net(TM) Designed by and Copyright Artistic Licence Holdings Ltd.
This library implements the published protocol ("Art-Net compatible");
no endorsement is implied.
*/

/**
Builds and reads Art-Net packets: DMX512 lighting levels and node discovery
over a network.

Send levels with <artnetBuildDmx>, which turns a universe number and up to
512 channel levels into one ArtDmx packet. Find the Art-Net nodes on a network
with <artnetBuildPoll>, and read each node's answer with <artnetParseReply>.
Read levels another controller sends with <artnetParseDmx>.

This library only turns values into Art-Net bytes and Art-Net bytes back into
values. The network is the stack's own: send the bytes with a datagram socket
(`open datagram socket`, then `write`) to port 6454, and receive them with
`accept datagram connections on port 6454 with message`. The artnet-helpers
script (examples/artnet-helpers.livecodescript) does both for you.

Nothing here throws for bad input. A refusal returns an empty result, and
<artnetLastError> says why.

Art-Net(TM) Designed by and Copyright Artistic Licence Holdings Ltd.

Tags: Networking, Art-Net, DMX, Lighting, Show control, Library
*/
library org.openxtalk.library.artnet

metadata title is "Art-Net compatible DMX for OpenXTalk"
metadata author is "Seth Morrow Software"
metadata version is "0.1.0"

private constant kOpDmx       is 20480   -- 0x5000
private constant kOpPoll      is 8192    -- 0x2000
private constant kOpPollReply is 8448    -- 0x2100
private constant kProtoVer    is 14

variable sLastError as String

-- =====================================================================
-- Byte helpers
-- =====================================================================
-- The 8-byte Art-Net ID: ASCII "Art-Net" + a NUL terminator.
private handler artnetId() returns Data
   variable tId as Data
   put the byte with code (65) into tId      -- A
   put the byte with code (114) after tId    -- r
   put the byte with code (116) after tId    -- t
   put the byte with code (45) after tId     -- -
   put the byte with code (78) after tId     -- N
   put the byte with code (101) after tId    -- e
   put the byte with code (116) after tId    -- t
   put the byte with code (0) after tId      -- NUL
   return tId
end handler

-- Pad (with zeros) or truncate channel Data to exactly pLen bytes.
-- (ShowControl's copy named its loop variable `i`: an all-lowercase LCB name
-- WARNS, and the IDE's Extension Builder compiles with -Werror, so the
-- extension could not be built there. Every name here has a capital.)
private handler fitChannels(in pChannels as Data, in pLen as Integer) returns Data
   variable tN as Integer
   variable tOut as Data
   variable tZero as Data
   variable tIndex as Integer
   put the number of bytes in pChannels into tN
   if tN is pLen then
      return pChannels
   end if
   if tN > pLen then
      return byte 1 to pLen of pChannels
   end if
   put pChannels into tOut
   put the byte with code (0) into tZero
   repeat with tIndex from tN + 1 up to pLen
      put tZero after tOut
   end repeat
   return tOut
end handler

-- One byte's value, or 0 past the end of the packet: every reader below goes
-- through this (or checks the length itself first), so no length a packet
-- claims can make the parser read beyond the bytes that arrived.
private handler byteAt(in pData as Data, in pIndex as Integer) returns Integer
   if pIndex < 1 or pIndex > the number of bytes in pData then
      return 0
   end if
   return the code of (byte pIndex of pData)
end handler

-- Read a fixed-width NUL-terminated ASCII field into a String. A field cut
-- short by the end of the packet reads to the end; a byte above 127 reads as
-- the Latin-1 character with that code (the specification says ASCII).
private handler fieldText(in pData as Data, in pStart as Integer, in pWidth as Integer) returns String
   variable tStr as String
   variable tIndex as Integer
   variable tByte as Integer
   put the empty string into tStr
   repeat with tIndex from pStart up to pStart + pWidth - 1
      if tIndex > the number of bytes in pData then
         exit repeat
      end if
      put the code of (byte tIndex of pData) into tByte
      if tByte is 0 then
         exit repeat
      end if
      put tStr & (the char with code (tByte)) into tStr
   end repeat
   return tStr
end handler

-- LCB has no integer-division operator ('div' is Script only and does not
-- parse in LCB). For non-negative integers a - (a mod b) is an exact multiple
-- of b, so dividing gives the exact quotient. (Defined before first use.)
private handler intDiv(in pA as Integer, in pB as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tQ as Integer
   put (pA - (pA mod pB)) / pB into tQ
   return tQ
end handler

-- Two lower-case hex digits for one byte value (a MAC address).
private handler hexByte(in pValue as Integer) returns String
   variable tDigits as String
   put "0123456789abcdef" into tDigits
   return (char (intDiv(pValue, 16) + 1) of tDigits) & (char ((pValue mod 16) + 1) of tDigits)
end handler

-- Are these the bytes of an Art-Net packet: the ID "Art-Net" + NUL, then at
-- least an OpCode?
private handler isArtNet(in pData as Data) returns Boolean
   if the number of bytes in pData < 10 then
      return false
   end if
   return (byte 1 to 8 of pData) is artnetId()
end handler

-- The OpCode of an Art-Net packet (little-endian, bytes 9 and 10).
private handler opCodeOf(in pData as Data) returns Integer
   return byteAt(pData, 9) + byteAt(pData, 10) * 256
end handler

-- =====================================================================
-- Output: ArtDmx
-- =====================================================================
/**
Summary: Builds one ArtDmx packet: the levels of one DMX universe, ready to send.

pUniverse: The universe (the 15-bit Port-Address), 0 to 32767.

pChannels: The levels as binary data, one byte (0 to 255) per DMX channel,
channel 1 first, up to 512 of them.

Returns: The packet as binary data, or empty when the universe is out of range.

Example:
local tLevels
put numToByte(255) & numToByte(128) & numToByte(0) into tLevels
open datagram socket to "192.168.1.50:6454"
write artnetBuildDmx(0, tLevels) to socket "192.168.1.50:6454"

Description: The packet carries an even number of channels from 2 to 512, as
the Art-Net specification asks: fewer than 2 levels, or an odd number, are
padded with level 0, and anything past 512 is left out. A universe outside
0 to 32767 builds nothing: the result is empty and <artnetLastError> says why.
A fractional universe is cut toward zero.

Every packet goes out with sequence number 0, which tells a node not to
reorder packets.
*/
public handler artnetBuildDmx(in pUniverse as Integer, in pChannels as Data) returns Data
   variable tLen as Integer
   variable tPkt as Data
   put the empty string into sLastError
   -- Refuse an out-of-range Port-Address BEFORE packing. LCB's mod follows the
   -- sign of the dividend, so a negative universe makes `the byte with code
   -- (pUniverse mod 256)` throw (out of the 0..255 byte domain), and one above
   -- 32767 would be silently masked into a different universe -- driving the
   -- wrong rig. Failure is quiet, never thrown.
   if pUniverse < 0 or pUniverse > 32767 then
      put "artnetBuildDmx: universe out of range 0..32767" into sLastError
      return the empty data
   end if
   put the number of bytes in pChannels into tLen
   if tLen > 512 then
      put 512 into tLen
   end if
   if tLen < 2 then
      put 2 into tLen
   end if
   if tLen mod 2 is 1 then
      put tLen + 1 into tLen
   end if

   put artnetId() into tPkt
   -- OpCode 0x5000, LITTLE-endian (low byte first)
   put the byte with code (kOpDmx mod 256) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (intDiv(kOpDmx, 256) mod 256) after tPkt
   -- Protocol version, BIG-endian (high byte first)
   put the byte with code (intDiv(kProtoVer, 256) mod 256) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (kProtoVer mod 256) after tPkt
   -- Sequence (0 = ordering disabled) + Physical (informational)
   put the byte with code (0) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (0) after tPkt
   -- SubUni (low byte) then Net (high 7 bits) of the 15-bit Port-Address
   put the byte with code (pUniverse mod 256) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (intDiv(pUniverse, 256) mod 128) after tPkt
   -- Length, BIG-endian (high byte first)
   put the byte with code (intDiv(tLen, 256) mod 256) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (tLen mod 256) after tPkt
   -- DMX data
   put fitChannels(pChannels, tLen) after tPkt
   return tPkt
end handler

-- =====================================================================
-- Input: ArtDmx
-- =====================================================================
/**
Summary: Reads an ArtDmx packet: the levels of one universe that arrived as bytes.

pData: The bytes of one datagram.

Returns: An array: "opcode" ("ArtDmx"), "universe" (0 to 32767 for a
well-formed packet), "net" and "subuni" (the two bytes the universe is made
of), "sequence", "physical", "length" (the number of channels) and "channels"
(the levels as binary data, channel 1 first). For bytes that are not an ArtDmx
packet, "opcode" is empty and <artnetLastError> says why.

Example:
put artnetParseDmx(pData) into tFrame
if tFrame["opcode"] is "ArtDmx" and tFrame["universe"] is 0 then
   put byteToNum(byte 1 of tFrame["channels"]) into tLevelOfChannel1
end if

Description: A packet whose Length field claims more channels than arrived, or
more than 512, is read as far as its bytes go and no further: "length" is the
number of levels in "channels".
*/
public handler artnetParseDmx(in pData as Data) returns Array
   variable tArr as Array
   variable tSeq as Integer
   variable tPhys as Integer
   variable tSub as Integer
   variable tNet as Integer
   variable tLen as Integer
   variable tAvail as Integer
   put the empty string into sLastError
   put the empty string into tArr["opcode"]
   if not isArtNet(pData) then
      put "artnetParseDmx: not an Art-Net packet" into sLastError
      return tArr
   end if
   if the number of bytes in pData < 18 then
      put "artnetParseDmx: packet too short" into sLastError
      return tArr
   end if
   if opCodeOf(pData) is not kOpDmx then
      put "artnetParseDmx: not an ArtDmx opcode" into sLastError
      return tArr
   end if
   put the code of (byte 13 of pData) into tSeq
   put the code of (byte 14 of pData) into tPhys
   put the code of (byte 15 of pData) into tSub
   put the code of (byte 16 of pData) into tNet
   -- Length is big-endian
   put the code of (byte 17 of pData) * 256 + the code of (byte 18 of pData) into tLen
   if tLen > 512 then
      put 512 into tLen           -- Art-Net DMX is 512 channels at most
   end if
   put the number of bytes in pData - 18 into tAvail
   if tLen > tAvail then
      put tAvail into tLen        -- never read past the bytes that arrived
   end if
   put "ArtDmx" into tArr["opcode"]
   put tSeq into tArr["sequence"]
   put tPhys into tArr["physical"]
   put tSub into tArr["subuni"]
   put tNet into tArr["net"]
   put tNet * 256 + tSub into tArr["universe"]
   put tLen into tArr["length"]
   if tLen > 0 then
      put byte 19 to (18 + tLen) of pData into tArr["channels"]
   else
      put the empty data into tArr["channels"]
   end if
   return tArr
end handler

-- =====================================================================
-- Discovery: ArtPoll / ArtPollReply
-- =====================================================================
/**
Summary: Builds an ArtPoll packet, which asks every Art-Net node to say who it is.

Returns: The packet as binary data.

Example:
set the allowDatagramBroadcasts to true
open datagram socket to "255.255.255.255:6454"
write artnetBuildPoll() to socket "255.255.255.255:6454"

Description: Broadcast it to port 6454 (the engine sends a broadcast only
after `set the allowDatagramBroadcasts to true`), or send it to one node's
address. Each node answers with an ArtPollReply, which <artnetParseReply>
reads. Nodes answer to port 6454 of the computer that asked, so listen there:
`accept datagram connections on port 6454 with message ...`.
*/
public handler artnetBuildPoll() returns Data
   variable tPkt as Data
   put the empty string into sLastError
   put artnetId() into tPkt
   -- OpCode 0x2000, little-endian
   put the byte with code (kOpPoll mod 256) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (intDiv(kOpPoll, 256) mod 256) after tPkt
   -- Protocol version, big-endian
   put the byte with code (intDiv(kProtoVer, 256) mod 256) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (kProtoVer mod 256) after tPkt
   -- Flags (0: answer only when polled) + DiagPriority (0)
   put the byte with code (0) after tPkt
   put the byte with code (0) after tPkt
   return tPkt
end handler

-- The universes (15-bit Port-Addresses) of a node's ports, from its
-- ArtPollReply: port N is an output when bit 7 of PortTypes[N] is set, an input
-- when bit 6 is, and its Port-Address is NetSwitch (7 bits), SubSwitch (4 bits)
-- and SwOut[N] or SwIn[N] (4 bits). pSwStart is the 1-based offset of SwOut
-- (191) or SwIn (187); PortTypes start at 175. A reply too short to hold the
-- port fields has no ports.
private handler portUniverses(in pData as Data, in pBit as Integer, in pSwStart as Integer) returns List
   variable tList as List
   variable tPort as Integer
   variable tType as Integer
   variable tBase as Integer
   put [] into tList
   if the number of bytes in pData < 194 then
      return tList
   end if
   put (byteAt(pData, 19) mod 128) * 256 + (byteAt(pData, 20) mod 16) * 16 into tBase
   repeat with tPort from 0 up to 3
      put byteAt(pData, 175 + tPort) into tType
      if (intDiv(tType, pBit) mod 2) is 1 then
         push tBase + (byteAt(pData, pSwStart + tPort) mod 16) onto tList
      end if
   end repeat
   return tList
end handler

/**
Summary: Reads an ArtPollReply packet: one node's answer to an ArtPoll.

pData: The bytes of one datagram.

Returns: An array: "opcode" ("ArtPollReply"), "ip" (the node's address, such
as "2.0.0.10"), "port" (6454), "shortName", "longName", "nodeReport" (the
node's status text), "net" and "subuni" (its Net and Sub-Net switches),
"outputUniverses" and "inputUniverses" (lists of the universes its DMX output
and input ports use), "mac" (such as "00:1a:2b:3c:4d:5e"), "style" (0 for a
node, 1 for a controller, 2 for a media server), "bindIndex" and "version"
(its firmware version). For bytes that are not an ArtPollReply, "opcode" is
empty and <artnetLastError> says why.

Example:
put artnetParseReply(pData) into tNode
if tNode["opcode"] is "ArtPollReply" then
   put tNode["shortName"] && "at" && tNode["ip"] into line (the number of lines of field "Nodes" + 1) of field "Nodes"
end if

Description: Send DMX for a node's output port to one of its
"outputUniverses". A node with more than four ports answers once per group of
four; "bindIndex" tells the answers apart.

A reply cut short (older nodes send fewer bytes) reads as far as it goes: a
field it does not reach is empty, or 0, or an empty list.
*/
public handler artnetParseReply(in pData as Data) returns Array
   variable tArr as Array
   variable tLen as Integer
   variable tMac as String
   variable tIndex as Integer
   put the empty string into sLastError
   put the empty string into tArr["opcode"]
   if not isArtNet(pData) then
      put "artnetParseReply: not an Art-Net packet" into sLastError
      return tArr
   end if
   put the number of bytes in pData into tLen
   if tLen < 26 then
      put "artnetParseReply: packet too short" into sLastError
      return tArr
   end if
   if opCodeOf(pData) is not kOpPollReply then
      put "artnetParseReply: not an ArtPollReply opcode" into sLastError
      return tArr
   end if
   put "ArtPollReply" into tArr["opcode"]
   -- IP address: 4 bytes at 11..14 (1-based). '&' joins Strings only, so each
   -- octet is formatted first.
   put (byteAt(pData, 11) formatted as string) & "." \
     & (byteAt(pData, 12) formatted as string) & "." \
     & (byteAt(pData, 13) formatted as string) & "." \
     & (byteAt(pData, 14) formatted as string) into tArr["ip"]
   -- Port: LITTLE-endian at 15..16
   put byteAt(pData, 15) + byteAt(pData, 16) * 256 into tArr["port"]
   -- VersInfoH, VersInfoL at 17..18 (big-endian)
   put byteAt(pData, 17) * 256 + byteAt(pData, 18) into tArr["version"]
   -- NetSwitch at 19, SubSwitch at 20 (ShowControl's names, kept)
   put byteAt(pData, 19) into tArr["net"]
   put byteAt(pData, 20) into tArr["subuni"]
   -- ShortName: 18 bytes at 27; LongName: 64 at 45; NodeReport: 64 at 109
   put fieldText(pData, 27, 18) into tArr["shortName"]
   put fieldText(pData, 45, 64) into tArr["longName"]
   put fieldText(pData, 109, 64) into tArr["nodeReport"]
   -- Ports: PortTypes at 175..178, SwIn at 187..190, SwOut at 191..194
   put portUniverses(pData, 128, 191) into tArr["outputUniverses"]
   put portUniverses(pData, 64, 187) into tArr["inputUniverses"]
   -- Style at 201; MAC (high byte first) at 202..207; BindIndex at 212
   put byteAt(pData, 201) into tArr["style"]
   put the empty string into tMac
   if tLen >= 207 then
      repeat with tIndex from 202 up to 207
         if tIndex > 202 then
            put tMac & ":" into tMac
         end if
         put tMac & hexByte(byteAt(pData, tIndex)) into tMac
      end repeat
   end if
   put tMac into tArr["mac"]
   put byteAt(pData, 212) into tArr["bindIndex"]
   return tArr
end handler

-- =====================================================================
-- Shared
-- =====================================================================
/**
Summary: Says why the last call of this library built or read nothing.

Returns: The reason, or empty when the last call succeeded.

Example:
put artnetBuildDmx(tUniverse, tLevels) into tPacket
if tPacket is empty then answer artnetLastError()

Description: Every other handler of this library clears it when it starts,
so it always describes the most recent call.
*/
public handler artnetLastError() returns String
   return sLastError
end handler

end library
